WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:02.701
-Our next guest
is a talented actor.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.537
You know from the film
"Operation Finale"

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.605
and the hit
Netflix series "Fauda."

00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:08.908
He co-created and stars
in "Hit &amp; Run,"

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.543
which is available now
on Netflix.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.711
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:21.721
♪♪

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:25.458
♪♪

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.327
[ Door slams ]
-What the [bleep]

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.529
[ Grunting ]

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.830
[ Crashing ]

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.866
[ Grunting ]

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:43.209
-Please welcome to the show
Lior Raz.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.111
♪♪

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.313
[ Applause ]

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.148
-There's not a lot
of talking here, yeah?

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:51.551
-Thank you.
-How are you doing?

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:55.254
♪♪

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:56.722
-Welcome to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:58.124
-It's very nice
to have you here.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.358
-Great to be here.

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:01.594
-So, you know,
you wrote this show, as well,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.029
so obviously,
you were aware, as an actor,

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:06.299
that you would be able
to pull off a scene like that.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:09.035
Is it fun to write it
knowing that you're gonna

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.369
be the one who gets to do it?

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:13.206
-You know when I wrote it,
me and Avi, my co-creator,

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.542
I thought -- we didn't know
that I would be the actor.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.643
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, and then Netflix

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:19.045
called us
and asked me to be there,

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.513
and it was great.
Yeah.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.815
-Netflix called me and said,
"We don't want you."

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:25.718
-Yeah, I asked them to do that.
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.120
So. you know, this is --

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.322
So, you have
a military background,

00:01:30.322 --> 00:01:32.758
and you have
a background doing security.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.393
-Yeah.
-And then, all of a sudden,

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:36.429
you sort of make this shift
late in life...

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.997
-Yeah.
-...into being an actor.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.832
-Right.
-How did it dawn on you

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.100
that that's
what you wanted to do?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.870
-So, I was -- as you said,
I worked in security.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.839
I was in the Special Forces
in Israel.

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:51.009
And then, I worked in, like,
a technology company in Israel.

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:54.847
One day, I met a girl, Katya.
And she looked at me,

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.615
and she said, "Why are you so
sad when you're going to work?"

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:58.484
And I said, "I'm not sad.
I'm very happy."

00:01:58.484 --> 00:01:59.752
And she said,
"No, I can see in your eyes

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.420
that you are very sad."

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.923
What would you do if I
gave you a billion dollars?"

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.791
I said, "Of course,
I'm gonna be an actor."

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:09.262
And she said, "Okay."
And she opened the Yellow Pages.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.398
Now you know how old I am.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:13.632
-She opened it, and she said,

00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:15.501
"This is the best
acting school in Israel.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.137
Let's call them."
So we called them.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.172
And then, since then,
I went there,

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.707
and it's --
I just became an actor.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:24.777
-And not just an actor.
You created --

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.113
The same co-writer. Yeah?
-Right, with Avi.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.148
-Avi and you create "Fauda"...
-Right.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.317
-...which is not only
a wildly popular show

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.319
in your home country
but then becomes

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.621
this sort of international hit.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:37.823
-And it must have been,
using your background

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:40.659
and writing a show like that,
I'm wondering,

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:44.129
you know, obviously,
you try to make it as realistic

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:45.865
as you remember it to be.
-Right.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.634
-Was it hard for you
to watch those kinds of shows

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.137
having that background,
the ones you didn't create,

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:52.371
did you ever watch them
and think,

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.707
"Oh, this isn't how it was"?
-Yeah, definitely.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:58.110
And also, the fighting scenes
and all the action scenes.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.712
When you see that,
you see that it's not --

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.147
it's not right.
You know?

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.782
In real life,
if you have a fight,

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:06.385
it's like it's supposed
to end in 30 seconds.

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:09.122
You know?
But in all those shows,

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.758
you have like two-minute,
three-minute fights.

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:15.428
And we have it -- and we tried
to do it as real as we can.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:18.097
Also, how they do all the,
you know --

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.000
how the Special Forces
actually act.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.903
And, you know, it's also --

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:27.072
When I was in the Special Forces
in undercover units.

00:03:27.072 --> 00:03:29.575
So you have to be an actor
over there, as well.

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:32.178
But you don't have second take
or third take or fourth take.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.212
-[ Laughing ] Sure.

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:35.114
-You have just one take,
and that's it.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.849
You're acting for your life.
It's crazy.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.085
-So this is --
We were talking backstage.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:42.321
You know, "Fauda," compared to
a lot of American productions,

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:44.757
even though
it looked really good,

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:48.027
a shoestring budget compared to
what you got to work with here.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.028
Plus, you shot
half of this in New York.

00:03:50.028 --> 00:03:51.964
What was your experience?

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:53.433
What were the biggest
differences for you,

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:56.335
getting to work
on an American production?

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:59.672
-So, in Israel,
you don't have budget at all.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:02.274
First of all.
It's, like, very low budget.

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:05.478
You can -- With "Hit &amp; Run,"
you know, we had so much.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:08.514
I could shoot like 10 "Faudas"

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:11.050
in one episodes
of "Hit &amp; Run."

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.485
But when you're shooting
in the U.S.,

00:04:13.485 --> 00:04:16.022
everybody knows
what they're doing. You know?

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.324
The photographer
is doing just that.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:19.859
The art doing just that.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:21.761
In Israel, everything is mixed.
You know?

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.330
So, one day, the boom man can
tell that you're getting fat.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.898
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:31.471
And the makeup artist can tell
you, "That was a bad scene.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.372
You wasn't so good in that.

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:35.040
You should ask to do it again."
You know?

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.309
-I just like that
you're describing my in-laws.

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:40.513
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:43.483
-You talked about the difference

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:45.484
that somebody could tell you
you're getting fat.

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:47.420
You know, but this did --

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.022
Like, one of the downsides
of COVID -- right? --

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.223
was, like,
people had to take breaks,

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:52.458
and people's bodies changed.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.493
And this actually
has happened to you.

00:04:54.493 --> 00:04:57.397
-Listen.
I was shooting here in New York.

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:59.198
We went to Israel.
The COVID started.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:02.167
We have to stop.
So I was in great shape.

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:05.137
So, during COVID,
I hurt my back,

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:07.573
I stopped smoking,
and I start baking.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:11.544
-Uh-huh.
-So it's like 15 pounds more.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:14.113
I was -- I gained 15 pounds.
And then they told me,

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:17.850
"In two months we go back.
We're shooting again in Israel."

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.419
So I had to lose 15 pounds
in two months.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:21.587
-But you're the writer.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.356
Why didn't you just
change your character?

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:25.558
-Because you have continuity,
you know?

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.326
-Oh, right.
That's it.

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:30.162
You shot all over New York City
to make this show.

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:31.830
-Right. Right.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.967
-Had you spent any time here
to that degree before?

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.637
-Yeah. I lived here for a while
when I was younger.

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:39.405
Yeah, I hated it
when I was younger.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.373
It was like --
It was too much for me.

00:05:41.373 --> 00:05:43.109
As you can see in "Hit &amp; Run,"

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:47.680
we tried to see how different
it is from Israel.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.316
Israel is much more light,
more blue and yellow.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.484
Here it was like,
everything is closing on you.

00:05:52.484 --> 00:05:55.421
I felt like a fish out of water
when I was young.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:58.724
And also,
this character that I'm doing,

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:01.627
you know, he's a fish
out of water in New York.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:03.362
-Gotcha.
-Yeah.

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.031
-As I mentioned, you know,
"Fauda" became this show

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:07.432
that started having
international appeal.

00:06:07.432 --> 00:06:10.136
I imagine you got recognized
a great deal in Israel,

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:12.671
but what happened to you
in sort of a

00:06:12.671 --> 00:06:15.707
maybe not perfect places
to get recognized.

00:06:15.707 --> 00:06:18.044
-Listen, I -- I came --
For the first time --

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:21.747
I didn't even know that
it's a big hit here, as well.

00:06:21.747 --> 00:06:23.382
So, I came, you know --

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:26.619
As an Israeli when you go to
immigration in the airport,

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.221
they're looking at you.

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.456
I feel guilty every time
that I'm there.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.358
They're asking you
some questions --

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.026
questions that I felt that,
you know?

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.495
So I was there,
and for the first time

00:06:36.495 --> 00:06:39.064
after "Fauda"
released on Netflix,

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:40.933
and I walked,
and I saw an officer

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:42.902
looking at me,
like, staring at me.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:45.137
And I said to myself,
"Come on, Lior.

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:46.873
You're gonna be there
like for hours now?

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:49.208
Interrogation
after interrogation."

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:52.778
So, I was standing in line,
and then I was the first one,

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:54.913
and I saw that she is free.

00:06:54.913 --> 00:06:57.015
So I told the guy behind me,
"No, you can go to her.

00:06:57.015 --> 00:06:58.684
It's okay.
I'm not in a hurry."

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.886
-[ Laughs ]
-And then she said --

00:07:00.886 --> 00:07:02.355
she looked at me and said,
"You, you, you, you!

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:05.190
Come right now, over here."
And I said, "Oh [bleep]"

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:09.228
I was sweating and everything.
And she looked at me,

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:11.263
and she said,
"So, when's the second season

00:07:11.263 --> 00:07:13.432
of 'Fauda' gonna release?"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:14.633
I said, "What?
Are you watching 'Fauda'?"

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:16.101
She said, "Yeah.
Everybody here watched 'Fauda.'"

00:07:16.101 --> 00:07:18.037
And then she said --
she said to all the officers,

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:20.072
"Look who's here!
Doron is here, Doron is here!"

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.774
-[ Laughs ]
-And then I went out.

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:24.643
I took an Uber, and it was,
like, an Indian driver

00:07:24.643 --> 00:07:28.080
that recognized my voice,
and he almost did an accident.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.416
"Doron, Doron, Doron!"
-[ Laughing ]

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:32.484
-So, yeah.
Everybody, yeah.

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:33.819
Many people recognize me now.
-Well, that's nice.

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:36.088
That's quite the accomplishment.
Not a lot of people

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:39.992
can shift gears into a career
as well and smoothly as you did.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.460
Congratulations on the new show,

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.894
and thanks so much for making
the time for us tonight.

00:07:42.894 --> 00:07:44.230
-Thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.232
-"Hit &amp; Run" is available now
on Netflix.

